std::expected is not modelled by the C++ front-end.  This test previously passed
only VACUOUSLY (the whole main body was dropped by the unsupported-construct
leniency, so nothing was verified).  The converting-fixed-parameter fix lets
more of std::expected instantiate, which now surfaces a real gap ("conversion
from 'void' to 'signed int'" in expected's internals) rather than silently
passing.  Flip back to CORE once std::expected is modelled.
